menuconfig ZMK_KEYSTATS
    bool "Per-key press counter"
    depends on SETTINGS
    depends on !ZMK_SPLIT || ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    help
      Count presses for every key position and keep the counts in
      persistent storage. On a split keyboard this runs on the central
      half, which sees the key events of both halves.

if ZMK_KEYSTATS

config ZMK_KEYSTATS_SAVE_INTERVAL
    int "Max seconds between flash saves while typing"
    default 600
    range 10 86400
    help
      Counts are written to flash at most once per interval while keys
      are being pressed, and additionally whenever the keyboard goes
      idle or to sleep. A hard power-off can lose up to this much
      typing.

config ZMK_KEYSTATS_BLE
    bool "GATT service to read and edit the counters"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_BLE
    help
      Expose the counters to bonded hosts through an encrypted GATT
      service that speaks newline-terminated JSON.

endif
